{
 "request": "Process the latest invoice from Sharma Logistics.",
 "goal": {
  "vendor_name": "Sharma Logistics"
 },
 "success": [
  "Invoice from Sharma Logistics processed"
 ],
 "lookups": [
  "find_vendors q='Sharma Logistics': 1 match(es): Sharma Logistics Pvt Ltd (id 1, approved)",
  "find_employees q='Sharma Logistics': 0 match(es)",
  "find_employees q='Sharma': 0 match(es)"
 ],
 "facts": {
  "vendor_id": 1,
  "mail_id": 7,
  "invoice_no": "INV-1043",
  "invoice_date": "2026-10-03",
  "due_date": "2026-11-02",
  "po_number": "PO-2026-0412",
  "subtotal_paise": "5288136 (Rs 52,881.36)",
  "tax_paise": "951864 (Rs 9,518.64)",
  "total_paise": "6240000 (Rs 62,400.00)",
  "source_file": "sharma_INV-1043.pdf"
 },
 "milestones": [
  {
   "id": "M1",
   "target": "The invoice from Sharma Logistics is entered in Acme with number INV-1043, dates 2026-10-03 and 2026-11-02, tax 951864, and total 6240000.",
   "sop_step": "PI-5",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_invoices",
     "args": {
      "vendor": 1
     },
     "where": {
      "invoice_no": "INV-1043",
      "vendor_id": 1
     },
     "expect": {
      "amount_paise": 6240000,
      "due_date": "2026-11-02",
      "invoice_date": "2026-10-03",
      "invoice_no": "INV-1043",
      "po_number": "PO-2026-0412",
      "tax_paise": 951864,
      "vendor_id": 1,
      "vendor_name": "Sharma Logistics"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M2",
   "target": "The source PDF file is attached to the invoice record.",
   "sop_step": "PI-6",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "get_invoice",
     "args": {
      "invoice_id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "where": {
      "id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "contains": {
      "source_file": [
       "sharma_INV-1043.pdf"
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M3",
   "target": "A pending business approval request exists for the invoice because the total exceeds Rs 50,000.",
   "sop_step": "PI-7",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_approvals",
     "args": {
      "status": "pending"
     },
     "where": {
      "entity_id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      },
      "entity_type": "invoice",
      "status": "pending"
     },
     "expect": {
      "entity_type": "invoice",
      "status": "pending"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M4",
   "target": "No payment request exists as a result of this run.",
   "sop_step": "PI-8",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_payments",
     "args": {
      "invoice": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "where": {
      "invoice_id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "count": 0
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}

Procedure:
### PI-5 Enter the invoice in Acme
- Target: one invoice record for the vendor exists with the cross-checked invoice number, dates, total and tax,
  each amount in paise. Acme sets the status from the total (ORG-001); the agent never sets it.
- Source: the cross-checked values; `POST /api/invoices` or the page `/invoices/new`.
- Ask when: Acme rejects a field and the correction is not obvious from its message.

### PI-6 Attach the source PDF
- Target: the invoice record shows the source PDF as its attached file. This is done through the UI only.
- Source: the file name from the message; the UI action `POST /invoices/{invoice_id}/attach-source`.
- Ask when: the attachment cannot be chosen unambiguously.

### PI-7 Request the business approval when required
- Target: if the invoice status is pending approval (total above Rs 50,000, ORG-001), exactly one pending
  business approval request exists for it; otherwise none. The agent never decides an approval.
- Source: the invoice status read back from Acme; `POST /api/approvals`.
- Ask when: an approval request for this invoice already exists in a state other than pending.

### PI-8 Leave everything else unchanged
- Target: no payment request, vendor change or bank-detail change exists as a result of this run.
- Source: `GET /api/audit` entries since the run started.
- Ask when: an unexpected change appears in the audit entries.

An independent check found these milestones unmet: M1 (0 matching row(s), expected 1); M2 (needs M1 first); M3 (needs M1, M2 first); M4 (needs M1, M2, M3 first). Records you already wrote stay: read before you write again.
